# Normalise to LF in the repository, and keep LF in the working tree too.
#
# `text=auto` alone only normalises what gets committed; on Windows,
# core.autocrlf=true still writes CRLF to disk. That makes PHP_CodeSniffer
# report Generic.Files.LineEndings.InvalidEOLChar on every source file, so the
# gate passes on Linux and fails on a developer's machine for reasons that have
# nothing to do with their change. `eol=lf` pins the checkout as well, which
# also matches the deploy target (PHP-FPM on Linux).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
